assets/0e38721ff6fe7b75bef46079d0c877333a0113cbc782a12f61e09b832200943a.png" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535143 true] [17592186333564 1111 #uuid "bfe8656e-f1db-5caf-8a21-48ef60b32eeb" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333566 13194139535143 true] [17592186333565 1089 "q-106946" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333565 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535143 true] [17592186333565 1100 "An eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ is  $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2c\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $c.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333565 1113 #uuid "a739e5b2-a47b-5126-9315-a2ade3bc34d8" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333565 1145 "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2c\\end{aligned}] & =3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2c\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1-4c \\\\ -2+8c\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6c\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1-4c=-3 \\\\ -2+8c=6c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n1-4c=-3\\,⟹\\,c=1.\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2+8c=6c\\,⟹\\,c=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $c=1.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333567 13194139535143 true] [17592186333566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333568 13194139535143 true] [17592186333566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333569 13194139535143 true] [17592186333566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333570 13194139535143 true] [17592186333566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333571 13194139535143 true] [17592186333566 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333566 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333566 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333569 13194139535143 true] [17592186333566 1110 #uuid "c7b58fca-a3bd-50c8-b716-40af28eeea21" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333567 1034 "3" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333567 1111 #uuid "fb6e56ea-0d61-55b9-8f84-eeacb7876fcd" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333568 1034 "6" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333568 1111 #uuid "5fea0568-fd79-54b6-b262-69c413e50d3a" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333569 1034 "1" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333569 1111 #uuid "fc315d45-49bc-5375-aee1-626dee300b16" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333570 1034 "0" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333570 1111 #uuid "858f42fe-fd05-5e56-bc2a-6b512d0a9592" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333571 1034 "-1" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333571 1111 #uuid "fdfc9749-7bb3-5732-b11e-fc007a2e1961" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333572 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333573 13194139535143 true] [17592186333572 1089 "q-107137" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333572 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535143 true] [17592186333572 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $v$ is an eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =5$ then $v$ is also an eigenvector of the matrix ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{5}.$\n- An eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =6$ is also an eigenvector of the inverse ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the same eigenvalue $\\lambda =6.$\n- If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2,$ then $7v$ is also an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =2.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333572 1113 #uuid "90a94767-f714-5ec0-8fe8-2166e2400350" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333572 1145 "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement is true. By the definition of an eigenvector, we have \n\n$$\nAv=5v.\n$$\n\n \nMultiplying it by ${A}^{-1}$ from the left, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=5{A}^{-1}v.\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $5$, we get \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}v=\\frac{1}{5}v.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $v$ is an eigenvector  of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\frac{1}{5}.$\n\n**Note:** In general, an eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to an eigenvalue $\\lambda $ is an eigenvector of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the statement above, an eigenvector of $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =6$ is an eigenvector of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{6}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(7v)=7Av=7(2v)=2(7v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(7v)=2(7v),$ and $7v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $7v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =2.$\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333574 13194139535143 true] [17592186333573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333575 13194139535143 true] [17592186333573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333576 13194139535143 true] [17592186333573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333577 13194139535143 true] [17592186333573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333578 13194139535143 true] [17592186333573 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333573 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333573 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333576 13194139535143 true] [17592186333573 1110 #uuid "97784497-097e-5492-8fdb-087a789773db" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333574 1034 "I,II, and III" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333574 1111 #uuid "1cc62fd0-3b60-57eb-8863-175b86f15892" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333575 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333575 1111 #uuid "050aeaf4-474e-55e2-ab64-880c94331f89" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333576 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333576 1111 #uuid "85645c94-69f7-593d-b964-e7d13a1fa4b2" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333577 1034 "III only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333577 1111 #uuid "d3f171a4-6f03-562c-bcaf-6ff6eddbbfc4" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333578 1034 "II only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333578 1111 #uuid "12acfd79-a1f3-5bd4-aa74-2c3e7718990b" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333579 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333580 13194139535143 true] [17592186333579 1089 "q-107819" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333579 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535143 true] [17592186333579 1100 "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 10\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333579 1113 #uuid "909b03c3-e39a-5b18-a828-a5284cd424be" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333579 1145 "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=4v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =4.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333581 13194139535143 true] [17592186333580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333582 13194139535143 true] [17592186333580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333583 13194139535143 true] [17592186333580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333584 13194139535143 true] [17592186333580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333585 13194139535143 true] [17592186333580 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333580 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333580 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333584 13194139535143 true] [17592186333580 1110 #uuid "df4de464-3831-5932-8664-eec48a32b93a" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333581 1034 "3" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333581 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333581 1111 #uuid "5c02a682-2a9c-5407-ac35-7dd5f73b0267" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333582 1034 "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333582 1111 #uuid "f99a5d98-82ee-5fb8-84ea-cb3f5f274ed8" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333583 1034 "-4" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333583 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333583 1111 #uuid "0aca831b-f409-5aa2-95e9-02ddde517ae6" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333584 1034 "4" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333584 1111 #uuid "84c16fc6-7bd1-57e5-940a-387679a83103" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333585 1034 "-2" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333585 1111 #uuid "b94c8553-8d5e-59f2-9938-a9ffbb4d45d5" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333586 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333587 13194139535143 true] [17592186333586 1089 "q-107837" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333586 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535143 true] [17592186333586 1100 "An eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -6 \\\\ -12 & 25\\end{aligned}]$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =7$ is  $v=[\\begin{aligned}c+1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $c.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333586 1113 #uuid "394982ad-ea62-5428-8f14-995c0f4069c3" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333586 1145 "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}11 & -6 \\\\ -12 & 25\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}c+1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}] & =7[\\begin{aligned}c+1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5c+11 \\\\ 13c-12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7c+7 \\\\ 7c\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5c+11=7c+7 \\\\ 13c-12=7c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n5c+11=7c+7\\,⟹\\,c=2.\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n13c-12=7c\\,⟹\\,c=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $c=2.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333588 13194139535143 true] [17592186333587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333589 13194139535143 true] [17592186333587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333590 13194139535143 true] [17592186333587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333591 13194139535143 true] [17592186333587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333592 13194139535143 true] [17592186333587 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333587 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333587 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333589 13194139535143 true] [17592186333587 1110 #uuid "5a658887-26f5-54db-bfce-82ec8034d797" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333588 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333588 1111 #uuid "6a18a2a3-5973-5132-8c42-b2a21fc869ae" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333589 1034 "2" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333589 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333589 1111 #uuid "5406d636-6ca2-505d-a7cf-d3fc9dcae63c" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333590 1034 "4" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333590 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333590 1111 #uuid "4714ba84-bb14-5b18-a5f9-f0fb0ec8743f" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333591 1034 "0" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333591 1111 #uuid "2ee5723e-a201-50d2-a717-0ecc63e3f9ff" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333592 1034 "-1" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333592 1111 #uuid "3e5c6f6b-daec-5dda-adb1-f2ce1f8742c1" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333593 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333594 13194139535143 true] [17592186333593 1089 "q-18233" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333593 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535143 true] [17592186333593 1100 "An eigenvector of $D=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 \\\\ -7 & 11\\end{aligned}]$ corresponding to an eigenvalue $\\lambda =6$ is  $[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $c.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333593 1113 #uuid "93364803-f932-5599-886a-b33bb951f95a" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333593 1145 "Remember that the eigenvectors of $D$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Dv=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Dv & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 \\\\ -7 & 11\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] & =6[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-8c+140 \\\\ -7c+154\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6c \\\\ 84\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-8c+140=6c \\\\ -7c+154=84\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-8c+140=6c\\,⟹\\,c=10.\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-7c+154=84\\,⟹\\,c=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $c=10.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333595 13194139535143 true] [17592186333594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333596 13194139535143 true] [17592186333594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333597 13194139535143 true] [17592186333594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333598 13194139535143 true] [17592186333594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333599 13194139535143 true] [17592186333594 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333594 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333594 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333595 13194139535143 true] [17592186333594 1110 #uuid "965f540b-5be5-5b7a-9514-ee1681c35330" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333595 1034 "10" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333595 1111 #uuid "8e721d1c-2b5d-5774-b4d1-305b4f6f7273" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333596 1034 "7" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333596 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333596 1111 #uuid "4b788941-acff-5edc-8fbc-6c557d5ffe45" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333597 1034 "14" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333597 1111 #uuid "77f6ae69-73a4-5bcf-a824-96a0026a0c89" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333598 1034 "1" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333598 1111 #uuid "533ea0a8-594b-5a20-af3f-dda0eb6c2e7c" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333599 1034 "5" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333599 1111 #uuid "07ce042c-ddf2-57a0-8e76-1832f4c73de4" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333600 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333601 13194139535143 true] [17592186333600 1089 "q-36678" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333600 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535143 true] [17592186333600 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $2.$\n- If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2,$ then $-v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =-2.$\n- $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $0.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333600 1113 #uuid "6af12d90-4cfe-54e1-b057-a8d41286b545" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333600 1145 "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=2v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(-v)=-Av=-(2v)=2(-v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(-v)=2(-v),$ and $-v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $-v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =2$ (but not $-2$).\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\n- Statement III is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=0v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139535143 true] [17592186333601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333602 13194139535143 true] [17592186333601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333603 13194139535143 true] [17592186333601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333604 13194139535143 true] [17592186333601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333605 13194139535143 true] [17592186333601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333606 13194139535143 true] [17592186333601 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333601 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333601 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333602 13194139535143 true] [17592186333601 1110 #uuid "f255a0b3-0887-5cad-ba83-f26df3e05d72" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333602 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333602 1111 #uuid "aaca6a4e-aefd-574a-8afb-a476135d2895" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333603 1034 "I only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333603 1111 #uuid "3f7c324b-ec86-5589-a079-7af025d55328" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333604 1034 "None" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333604 1111 #uuid "3bfaaa5e-dc74-5742-95e5-436b2715d23b" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333605 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333605 1111 #uuid "1b23df11-6b55-5c47-8402-d911a1800e82" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333606 1034 "II only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333606 1111 #uuid "c5317a8b-5c94-5072-9b2e-8d4bfda5b32c" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333607 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333608 13194139535143 true] [17592186333607 1089 "q-36865" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333607 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535143 true] [17592186333607 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $v$ is an eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ then $v$ is also an eigenvector of the matrix ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{3}.$\n- An eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ is also an eigenvector of the inverse ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the same eigenvalue $\\lambda =2.$\n- If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3,$ then $5v$ is also an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =-3.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333607 1113 #uuid "aae12eda-62c6-5db8-83be-eba7232a765e" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333607 1145 "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. By the definition of an eigenvector, we have \n\n$$\nAv=3v.\n$$\n\n \nMultiplying it by ${A}^{-1}$ from the left, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=3{A}^{-1}v.\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $3$, we get \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}v=\\frac{1}{3}v.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $v$ is an eigenvector  of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\n**Note:** In general, an eigenvector of an invertible matrix $A$ that corresponds to an eigenvalue $\\lambda $ is an eigenvector of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the statement above, an eigenvector of $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvector of ${A}^{-1}$ that corresponds to $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(5v)=5Av=5(-3v)=-3(5v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(5v)=-3(5v),$ and $5v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $5v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-3.$\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333609 13194139535143 true] [17592186333608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333610 13194139535143 true] [17592186333608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333611 13194139535143 true] [17592186333608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333612 13194139535143 true] [17592186333608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333613 13194139535143 true] [17592186333608 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333608 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333608 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333610 13194139535143 true] [17592186333608 1110 #uuid "6c82669f-d84e-5499-9337-132d6c303242" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333609 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333609 1111 #uuid "122875ce-dbc1-54af-8cb3-cb09cc02ae34" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333610 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333610 1111 #uuid "93894d11-c361-5010-b3cb-705ff9b5d53d" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333611 1034 "III only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333611 1111 #uuid "c796dfd5-92b9-59fb-8447-cc9d8ff4fded" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333612 1034 "None" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333612 1111 #uuid "541acfa6-7766-5bd7-af1d-d460e739123f" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333613 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333613 1111 #uuid "ad7f4ecf-0acb-5f55-a8e8-5ced03a8a965" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333614 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333615 13194139535143 true] [17592186333614 1089 "q-36869" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333614 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535143 true] [17592186333614 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/0fb9b5442b5721d4dc273978f30fa79d5b5555faac0672ea44e11ebf79387d6c.png)\n\nThe vector $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $1.$ Find the vector $Av.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333614 1113 #uuid "885a86b4-4c0a-595d-852f-a00f02fd8acf" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333614 1145 "The eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =1v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/221b02b2df0cd292a41593f52b96be20c0ed20c1b1ccad080157f4729d871f0c.png)" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333616 13194139535143 true] [17592186333615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333617 13194139535143 true] [17592186333615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333618 13194139535143 true] [17592186333615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333619 13194139535143 true] [17592186333615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333620 13194139535143 true] [17592186333615 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333615 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333615 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333620 13194139535143 true] [17592186333615 1110 #uuid "822f3073-ebee-579a-aa95-00660941f6a5" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333616 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/3c202b0f2c679121f4c51a57514aea8a8d6bf5706e67e4d8986b9ec624a74574.png" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535143 true] [17592186333616 1111 #uuid "ca64db74-26d1-581e-9a2c-e81c3427a66c" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333617 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/e56f6feb61896097941f2df3ff6b38dff9972820180f571383635d29b95ba8bc.png" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535143 true] [17592186333617 1111 #uuid "44747833-254d-5f13-a47a-98bd83b202fa" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333618 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/8e53fd4d2bcde7cbe59d4be00f8e6a14a9f3bc979388791c46e0faef3d51d158.png" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535143 true] [17592186333618 1111 #uuid "0d7beb28-e356-52a3-a852-c95cdfa64e05" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333619 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/7e74dbc626472e00e42db273ef7d005ec9b3103f8708214871912382fed66663.png" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535143 true] [17592186333619 1111 #uuid "fdf3aa9a-7904-5f73-8cb0-7b6d870e601c" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333620 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/221b02b2df0cd292a41593f52b96be20c0ed20c1b1ccad080157f4729d871f0c.png" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535143 true] [17592186333620 1111 #uuid "a856b48d-97ef-598d-9795-28f3fcb1137e" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333622 13194139535143 true] [17592186333621 1089 "q-37090" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535143 true] [17592186333621 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $5$ then $10v$ is also an eigenvector corresponding to $5.$\n- $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $6.$\n- $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $4.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333621 1113 #uuid "871a89c7-3af9-5b70-b051-4f7fed74e27c" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333621 1145 "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(10v)=10Av=10(5v)=5(10v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(10v)=5(10v),$ and $10v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $10v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5.$\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\n- Statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=6v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =6.$\n\n- Statement III is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=4v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139535143 true] [17592186333622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333623 13194139535143 true] [17592186333622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333624 13194139535143 true] [17592186333622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333625 13194139535143 true] [17592186333622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333626 13194139535143 true] [17592186333622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333627 13194139535143 true] [17592186333622 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333622 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333622 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333623 13194139535143 true] [17592186333622 1110 #uuid "41fdd86d-1d05-5807-a30a-fb5f7bfa20cb" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333623 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333623 1111 #uuid "a85bca4c-844d-5930-b624-471f31e71e40" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333624 1034 "III only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333624 1111 #uuid "b548fd6f-e362-5cb9-abd4-329ba153de76" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333625 1034 "None" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333625 1111 #uuid "57731619-6376-5f0a-a424-c82749eeb377" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333626 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333626 1111 #uuid "11fcfe37-2def-53e2-aed3-15a5bbfecfaa" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333627 1034 "II only" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333627 1111 #uuid "506576fd-c46f-5f76-8a9e-0551f748436e" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333628 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333629 13194139535143 true] [17592186333628 1089 "q-70917" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333628 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535143 true] [17592186333628 1100 "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333628 1113 #uuid "740777a5-43a4-5203-8f0b-72f91859f44e" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333628 1145 "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $v$ is an eigenvector, then there must exist a real number $\\lambda $ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis leads to the following system of equations for $\\lambda :$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2=2\\lambda  \\\\ 3=-\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has no solution. Therefore, $v$ is not an eigenvector of $A.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333630 13194139535143 true] [17592186333629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333631 13194139535143 true] [17592186333629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333632 13194139535143 true] [17592186333629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333633 13194139535143 true] [17592186333629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333634 13194139535143 true] [17592186333629 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333629 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333629 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333630 13194139535143 true] [17592186333629 1110 #uuid "9ee20386-319d-5f3f-9497-b8386be5dbc3" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333630 1034 "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333630 1111 #uuid "5952ab21-3b0c-50b9-913b-305ff7c06b67" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333631 1034 "2" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333631 1111 #uuid "a2697a81-d07b-54e2-808d-a906b013899a" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333632 1034 "1" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333632 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333632 1111 #uuid "0e40e7bc-64dc-58df-8e7b-9aae720090bf" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333633 1034 "-3" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333633 1111 #uuid "8c0f7913-f9a3-5e9c-9c60-430574c79c6c" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333634 1034 "0" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333634 1111 #uuid "09721ffc-5370-5014-9cba-533e43e4db02" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333635 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333636 13194139535143 true] [17592186333635 1089 "q-75589" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333635 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535143 true] [17592186333635 1100 "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333635 1113 #uuid "700440da-12e4-50fe-86c5-d292870ad78e" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333635 1145 "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $v$ is an eigenvector, then there must exist a real number $\\lambda $ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]=\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis leads to the following system of equations for $\\lambda :$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}11=3\\lambda  \\\\ 13=-2\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has no solution. Therefore, $v$ is not an eigenvector of $A.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333637 13194139535143 true] [17592186333636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333638 13194139535143 true] [17592186333636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333639 13194139535143 true] [17592186333636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333640 13194139535143 true] [17592186333636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333641 13194139535143 true] [17592186333636 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333636 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333636 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333639 13194139535143 true] [17592186333636 1110 #uuid "70547335-d416-5207-aba4-5d79c2b8d945" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333637 1034 "-\\frac{13}{2}" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333637 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333637 1111 #uuid "b59e3321-188d-5167-b2d0-db7db8656153" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333638 1034 "3" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333638 1111 #uuid "1cc86d0c-6652-5585-8c8e-801a21c7fcae" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333639 1034 "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535143 true] [17592186333639 1111 #uuid "5a878ef1-ea20-5e0a-a290-00309d277797" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333640 1034 "\\frac{11}{3}" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333640 1111 #uuid "070a7758-3716-5b99-b438-d604be8b25ba" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333641 1034 "4" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333641 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333641 1111 #uuid "a1dc343e-6533-5d79-83a8-e4fb1462f063" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333642 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333643 13194139535143 true] [17592186333642 1089 "q-75610" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333642 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535143 true] [17592186333642 1100 "An eigenvector of \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}]$ \ncorresponding to an eigenvalue $\\lambda =5k-4$ is $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3k-1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333642 1113 #uuid "a7f901fa-248f-5ae5-86ed-bb1e2ea109ca" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333642 1145 "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3k-1\\end{aligned}] & =(5k-4)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3k-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2+2(3k-1) \\\\ -10+8(3k-1)\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2(5k-4) \\\\ (5k-4)(3k-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6k \\\\ 24k-18\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10k-8 \\\\ 15{k}^{2}-17k+4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6k=10k-8 \\\\ 24k-18=15{k}^{2}-17k+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n6k=10k-8\\,⟹\\,k=2.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $k=2$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24k-18 & =15{k}^{2}-17k+4 \\\\ 24\\cdot 2-18 & =15\\cdot {2}^{2}-17\\cdot 2+4 \\\\ 30 & =30,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a true statement.\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=2.$" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333644 13194139535143 true] [17592186333643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333645 13194139535143 true] [17592186333643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333646 13194139535143 true] [17592186333643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333647 13194139535143 true] [17592186333643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333648 13194139535143 true] [17592186333643 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535143 true] [17592186333643 1041 "selection" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333643 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333644 13194139535143 true] [17592186333643 1110 #uuid "cce53c32-fd8c-59de-8a66-cc917fff76c9" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333644 1034 "2" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333644 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333644 1111 #uuid "0a7a572b-76f3-5005-96a4-612f4632f248" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333645 1034 "6" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333645 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333645 1111 #uuid "d8354623-60bd-5c96-b3ee-a96c0914763b" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333646 1034 "1" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333646 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333646 1111 #uuid "509d9686-b782-5098-8d44-67d9307adb25" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333647 1034 "-2" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333647 1111 #uuid "f21a93e6-e6c6-52e5-8094-d37f812e5250" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333648 1034 "-6" 13194139535143 true] [17592186333648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535143 true] [17592186333648 1111 #uuid "f4fa832a-6af9-55f6-8d16-c29a44ab45e0" 131941